think stacks like books on shell!
you can stack a bunch of books on top each other
but we can only view or remove the top book!
if we want first book, we should remove book one by one.
we call this "LAST IN, FIRST OUT" or "LIFO PRINCIPLE"


internally, we use a Array or Linked-List to store the obj in stacks.
so a Stack is basically a "WRAPPER" around an array or linked-list,
that gives us a different way of storing and accessing objects (rather than linked-list and arrays
Stack in Java (java.util) is array based!


stacks have 4 operations
push/pop/peek/isEmpty

important note: the main goal of stack
                is all functionalities (push/pop/peek/isEmpty)
                is O(1)
                even ArrayBasedStack or LinkedListStack
                all of them is O(1)
                THIS IS MAIN PROPERTY OF STACK!

Note: we have not any functionalities for search or lookup
      because stacks is not for that!
      if you want to search on a stack, think again!
      MAYBE YOU SHOULD CHANGE DATA STRUCTURE!

we use Stack data structure for

1.implementing "UNDO" feature
  because we can find pre item immediately

2.implementing compilers to syntax checking
  like what we do in 4.4 for balanced expressions

3.evaluate arithmetic expressions like calculator
  because can find the order like (1+2*3)

4.impleting navigations
  like forward/backward move
  like forward/backward in browsers


